      "key": "WORK-1321",
      "summary": "Add a new shipment status \"Tendered\"",
      "description": "Background\nWe are moving the warehouse from DISH to Arcadia, a 3P warehouse. With the operational changes with the new warehouse, there’s the need for ops team to have a new shipment status to accommodate the operational change.\nRequirement\nhttps://www.figma.com/design/1t5h8AfmPqjqGTb8oDeRxC/Wonder-for-Business-OMS?node-id=3557-2126&t=mmcC7DsJikj3q1gk-4\n \nAdd a new shipment status “Tendered” for shipments whose order_type is Food.\nThis new status will mean that the logistics pull report, which is going to be built in \nhttps://wonder.atlassian.net/browse/WORK-1317\n, has been emailed to the 3P warehouse.\nThis new status will go before Picked, so the flow of the shipment status will be Open → Tendered → Picked → Shipped → Delivered. \nThe Tendered shipment status will not update the order status. In other words, even though the shipment status is at Tendered, the order status will remain at Confirmed.\nStatus will be updated manually by Ops team.\nShipment status can be updated from two places:\nThe All Shipments page. In this page, use can select all shipments that are at the status of “Open”, and then click on the Load Tendered button, which is also a new button to be added.\nWhen clicking on the Load Tendered button, show a hopup “Mark the load as Tendered”. \nOnce user clicks on the Save button, change the status of the shipment to Tendered. \nA new permission control Shipment Status Update will be added to control the permission of this button. The permission shall be assigned to Logistics team.\nThe Shipment Details page. \nWhen the shipment status is Open, enable the progress button.\nWhen clicking on the progress button, show the Mark the load as Tendered hopup.\nWhen the shipment status is Picked, disable the progress button if the Pikced in this shipment field is empty for all the shipment items.",
