      "summary": "Dispatch CK->SD1+ARC Orders to SPORK",
      "description": "Timeline\nProduction ready before \n2026-07-13\nContext\nWe need to expand our whitelist of enabled routes for production.\nMost urgently, the use cases include:\nIn order to meet COGS goals by end of year, we need production to imminently ship product to \nArcadia\n. Teams will be shipping manually starting July 1, however are hoping for a systemic solve by July 13.\nWe also need to support CK1 > SD1 route to unblock SD1 launch slated fall 2026.\nHowever, we want this “eligible production” receiver list to be flexible as we anticipate a larger suite of customers over time. \nUltimately, we expect that whitelisted route POs (CK1 > DISH, CK1 > SD1, CK1 > Arcadia) must be dispatched to \nSPORK\n so receiver facilities can receive/produce against them. Today the \ndispatcher gate-keeps (suppresses) routes other than Production Node→DISH dispatch in code\n. This ticket enables that path for SD1 and Arcadia. Owner: Sahil Vora.\nRequirement\nDevelop a flexible route whitelist that we can easily update over time.\nEnable the dispatcher to send POs for the following routes to SPORK:\nProduction Node > SD1 (*Texas dish)\nProduction Node > Arcadia\nAcceptance Criteria\nCK1→Arcadia POs placed in POMS are dispatched to SPORK (ezbake) like existing CK→DISH dispatches.\nCK1→SD1 POs placed in POMS are dispatched to SPORK (ezbake) like existing CK→DISH dispatches.\nThe CK1→DC dispatch gate is removed/flag-controlled for the \nSD1\n and \nArcadia \nnodes only — other routes unchanged.\nAck signals flow back (SPORK → SporkLift → POMS) as they do for current CK→DISH.\nValidated in the \nUAT shadow test\n (parent SUPPLY-3130) before enabling in prod.\nTechnical notes\nDispatcherService.dispatchOrders\n — locate and flag the existing CK1→DC suppression gate.\nezbake PurchaseOrder proto already carries \nsupplier_id\n / \nreceiver_id\n / \norder_number\n (SUPPLY-3100); receiver = SD1 & Arcadia node.\nResolve SD1 & Arcadia node identity (Command Center node).\nEdge cases\nScope strictly to Production Node→SD1 and Production Node → Arcadia  — don't open other routes prematurely.\nIdempotent dispatch; correct supplier/receiver node mapping.",
