    "content": {
      "value": "**1. Context & Objective**\n--------------------------\n\nArcadia serves as Wonder’s 3PL partner, managing both **Wonder 1P (HDR crusts)** and **B2B (3P vendor)** inventory.  \nThe goal is to transition all inventory ownership and management flows from **OrderGrid (OG)** to **ShipHero (SH)**, ensuring accurate, systematic handling of inventory, transfers, and lot/expiration tracking.\n\n**Key Objectives**\n\n* Replace unreliable OG data with ShipHero as the new system of record.\n* Align SKU and UOM structures across Arcadia and DISH.\n* Establish clean, auditable inventory transactions.\n* Enable perpetual inventory tracking with consistent reconciliation.\n\n**2. Data Management & System Setup**\n-------------------------------------\n\n### **Initial Setup**\n\n| Step | Description | Owner | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Arcadia warehouse setup | Create and activate Arcadia warehouse in SH | @Kshitij Mate | Done |\n| SKU setup | Create all required SKUs (88\\*, VSKU) in SH | @Kshitij Mate | Pending |\n| Inventory upload | Upload Arcadia’s on-hand inventory snapshot (as of 9/30 and current) via CSV | @Emmett Garber  (Need RMX sku to WOnder sku mapping from @Emmett Garber ) | Blocked (Need RMX sku to WOnder sku mapping from @Emmett Garber) |\n| Lot/Expiration mapping | SH Support to associate Lots and Expirations | SH Support | Pending |\n| OG inventory wipe | Wipe all OG inventory post-upload | @Kshitij Mate | Pending |\n\n**Method:**\n\n* CSV bulk upload to initialize SH inventory.\n* ShipHero support required to associate lots/expirations (process may take several days).\n\n**Timeline:**\n\n* Pending Finance sign-off.\n\n**OrderGrid Status:**\n\n* Data has been unreliable for several months.\n* Plan: Wipe OG data entirely post-upload to SH.\n\n**Starting Point:**\n\n* Emmet to provide inventory snapshots from 9/30 and current date.\n\n### **3. SKU Structure & Unit of Measurement (UOM)**\n\n### **Newark / HDR Crusts (1P)**\n\n* **Current State:** Arcadia maintains inventory at case level.\n* **Decision:** Maintain inventory as cases at Arcadia, then break down to eaches upon receiving at DISH.\n* **Rationale:** Mirrors beverage breakdown process; serves as a training opportunity for the DISH team.\n* **Example:** `8801234-15` = Case of 15 eaches of SKU `8801234`.\n* **Transfer Orders:** Created at case level, received as eaches at DISH.\n\n### **B2B 88\\* Items**\n\n* **Status:** Maintained at case level in Arcadia.\n* **Decision:** No change.\n* **Gap:** No sales order creation in SH for B2B (planned for Q4, not yet prioritized).\n* **Impact:** No transaction logs for picks; current manual workaround continues.\n\n### **Vendor SKUs (3P)**\n\n* **Structure:** Use PO default UOM consistently across systems.\n* **Alignment:** Arcadia inventory, POs, and transfers use same UOM.\n* **Current Plan:** Continue using vendor SKUs, then transition to 88\\* format later, aligned with DISH rollout.\n\n**Open Questions:**\n\n* None currently — UOM decisions finalized in last meeting.\n\n**4. Purchase Order Management**\n--------------------------------\n\n### **Cutover from OrderGrid**\n\n* 8 open POs identified in Arcadia OG.\n\n**Cutover Plan**\n\n1. **Cancel** OG POs with delivery dates post go-live.\n2. **Recreate** them in ShipHero with new PO numbers.\n3. **Notify suppliers** to reference new PO numbers on invoices.\n4. Add **original OG PO numbers** as notes in SH POs.\n5. **Hand-hold** first few receipts to ensure team alignment on PO mappings.\n\n**Post-Go-Live Operations**\n\n| Role | Responsibility |\n| --- | --- |\n| @Jennifer Snyder @María Jumbo Flores | Create all Arcadia POs in SH |\n| @Emmett Garber | Remotely receive POs in SH |\n| **RMX** | Physically receive inventory at Arcadia |\n| @Emmett Garber | Close POs after receipt — critical for forecasting accuracy |\n\n**5. Transfer Order Process**\n-----------------------------\n\n**Workflow**\n\n1. Transfer recommendations generated from planning sheet/system (TBD).\n2. Emmet manually creates Transfer Orders in SH.\n3. SH auto-generates a receiving PO at DISH.\n4. Emmet picks, packs, and ships (no scanners, laptop only).\n5. DISH receives both physically and in SH.\n\n**Schedule**\n\n* **Mon → Wed:** Order Monday for Wednesday receipt\n* **Wed → Fri:** Order Wednesday for Friday receipt\n* **Thu → Mon:** Optional (for weekend volumes)\n* **Lead Time:** 2 days standard\n\n**Data Access**\n\n* Emmet will use a lightweight lookup/download tool for transfer SKUs and quantities.\n* Parameters configurable in backend sheet.\n\n**6. Inventory Reconciliation & Accuracy**\n------------------------------------------\n\n**Frequency**\n\n* Weekly checks for first month, then monthly after stabilization.\n\n**Method**\n\n* Compare SH inventory vs Arcadia Excel data.\n* Use SH cycle counting for targeted corrections — no full re-uploads.\n* Create RCA tickets for large discrepancies.\n* Maintain perpetual inventory tracking (target 99% accuracy).\n\n**7. Reason Codes**\n-------------------\n\n| Type | Description | Example |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Initial Upload | Used for SH inventory initialization | “ShipHero Inventory Initialization” |\n| Ongoing | Use below SH’s 10 predefined reason codes | Batch Pull |\n|  |  | Cycle Count |\n|  |  | Damaged Items |\n|  |  | Discontinued |\n|  |  | Expired |\n|  |  | Incorrect Receiving |\n|  |  | Inventory not available |\n|  |  | Other - Please use text box |\n|  |  | Production (remove from system) |\n|  |  | Quality |\n\n**8. Data Sync & Visibility**\n-----------------------------\n\n* Same BQ tables as existing DISH setup.\n* Arcadia inventory differentiated via warehouse ID in Command center nodes table.\n* Purchase Orders appear in existing BQ PO table.\n* Inventory shown in shared snapshot table.\n\n**9. Operational SOPs**\n-----------------------\n\n### **Transfers (Arcadia → DISH)**\n\n* Performed manually by Emmet in SH.\n* Auto-generates POs for DISH.\n* Ensures systematic, auditable transactions.\n* Avoids manual uploads and maintains lot/expiration integrity.\n* FEFO depletion logic aligned across both Arcadia and SH.\n\n### **Inventory Adjustments**\n\n* Arcadia to provide daily exports of expired/damaged inventory.\n* Emmet to manually mirror adjustments in SH.\n* Future: Consider automated sync via integration.\n\n**Open Question**\n\n* Will Arcadia perform periodic physical counts, and how will they be reconciled with SH?\n\n### **B2B Integration Plan (TBD)**\n\n* ~~In mid/end Q4, we will work on integrating POMS (Purchase Order Management System) with WOMS (Wonder Works Order Management System) to automate B2B order flow:~~\n\n  + ~~B2B orders from WOMS will flow into POMS~~\n  + ~~From there, they will be passed to ShipHero via SPORKLIFT.~~\n  + ~~Emmett’s team will pack and ship orders directly within ShipHero, without the need for bin/location scanning.~~\n  + ~~This will ensure accurate inventory depletion & shipping records and will simplify operational overhead while maintaining data integrity.~~\n  + ~~We will not use lot and exp set up for B2B~~\n* B2B skus will be handled in a similar way as the HDR crusts.\n* Inv will be uploaded on the 88\\* CS UOMs without the Lots and Expirations.\n* **No order creations in SH for inv consumption.**\n* We will deplete Inv daily/weekly based on whatever is shipped out of Arcadia by RMX.\n* Add Reason code to explicitly signal **B2B order consumption**.\n* Expirations and Damages will be handled with their own reason codes and not mixed with ^.\n\nMeeting Notes\n=============\n\nKey Decisions & Alignments\n--------------------------\n\n### 1. **Inventory Upload & Initialization**\n\n* **Method**: CSV bulk upload to initialize Ship Hero system\n* **Timeline**: Awaiting finance sign-off (Monday meeting scheduled)\n* **Ownership**: Kshitij and Emmet will execute together\n* **Critical Issue**: Ship Hero support needed to associate lots and expirations (may take several days)\n* **Starting Point**: Emmet to provide inventory snapshot as of 9/30 and current date\n* **Ordergrid Status**: Inventory data unreliable for several months; being wiped out completely\n\n### 2. **SKU Structure & Unit of Measurement (UOM)**\n\n#### **Newark/HDR Crusts (1P)**\n\n* **Current State**: Arcadia maintains inventory at case level\n* **Decision**: Switch to tracking as cases at Arcadia, then break down to eaches at Dish upon receiving\n* **Rationale**: Mirrors existing beverage breakdown process; uses this as training opportunity for Dish team\n* **Example**: SKU 8801234-15 would represent a case of 15 units of 8801234\n* **Transfer Orders**: Will be created at case level, broken down upon receipt at Dish\n\n#### **B2B 88\\* Items**\n\n* **Status**: Maintained at case level at Arcadia\n* **No Change**: Will continue as case-level inventory\n* **Important Gap**: No sales order creation in Ship Hero for B2B (planned for Q4 but not prioritized)\n* **Impact**: No transaction logs for picks until feature implemented; continues current workaround\n\n#### **Vendor SKUs (3P)**\n\n* **Structure**: Using Purchase Order default UOM consistently across all systems\n* **Alignment**: Arcadia inventory, POs, and transfer orders all use same UOM\n* **Current State**: Will use vendor SKUs initially; transition to 88\\* format later (aligned with Dish transition)\n\n### 3. **Purchase Order Management**\n\n#### **Open POs in Ordergrid**\n\n* **Current Status**: 8 open POs identified in Arcadia OG\n* **Cutover Plan**:\n\n  + Cancel all OG POs with delivery dates after go-live\n  + Recreate in Ship Hero with new PO numbers\n  + Contact suppliers to reference new PO numbers on invoices\n  + Create notes on Ship Hero POs referencing original OG PO numbers\n* **Dock Receiving**: Hand-hold initial receipts; inform receiving team of PO mapping\n\n#### **Going Forward**\n\n* Jen and Maria will create purchase orders for Arcadia in Ship Hero\n* Emmet will remotely receive them in Ship Hero\n* RMX will physically receive inventory at Arcadia\n* Emmet responsible for closing out POs after receipt (critical for accurate inventory forecasting)\n\n### 4. **Transfer Order Process**\n\n#### **Workflow**\n\n1. System (TBD) generates transfer order recommendations for Emmet\n2. Emmet (or team) manually creates transfer orders in Ship Hero\n3. Transfer order auto-generates corresponding receiving order/PO at Dish\n4. Emmet picks, packs, and ships (no scanning required; laptop-based)\n5. Dish team receives inventory physically and in Ship Hero\n\n#### **Schedule**\n\n* **Monday → Wednesday**: Order Monday for Wednesday receipt\n* **Wednesday → Friday**: Order Wednesday for Friday receipt\n* **Thursday → Monday**: Optional for weekend volume\n* **Lead Time**: 2 days consistently\n\n#### **Data Delivery**\n\n* Lightweight lookup/download system for Emmet to access transfer quantities and SKUs\n* Parameters easily adjustable in backend sheet\n\n### 5. **Inventory Reconciliation & Accuracy**\n\n#### **Frequency**\n\n* **Initial Proposal**: Monthly validation/cycle counts\n* **Concern Raised**: May be too infrequent given Ship Hero launch experience\n* **Recommendation**: More frequent checks in first month to catch issues early\n\n#### **Method**\n\n* Compare Ship Hero inventory to Arcadia Excel files\n* Use cycle counting in Ship Hero to true up discrepancies\n* Not full re-upload; targeted adjustments only\n* Separate RCA process for significant variances\n\n#### **Perpetual Inventory**\n\n* System will function as perpetual inventory (99% accuracy goal)\n* Cycle counts used to correct discrepancies, not replace perpetual tracking\n\n### 6. **Reason Codes**\n\n* **Initial Upload**: \"Ship Hero Inventory Initialization\" reason code\n* **Ongoing**: 12 different reason codes available including:\n\n  + Damages\n  + Expirations\n  + Quality Control\n\n### 7. **Data Sync & Inventory Tables**\n\n* Same tables as current Dish operations\n* Different warehouse ID distinguishes Arcadia inventory\n* Purchase orders visible in existing PO table\n* Inventory visible in existing inventory snapshot table\n\nOpen Items & Follow-ups\n-----------------------\n\n### **Before Go-Live**\n\n1. Finance sign-off meeting (Monday)\n2. Emmet to provide inventory snapshots (9/30 and current)\n3. Example flow documentation for Newark crust case-to-each conversion\n4. Supplier notifications for PO number changes (8 vendors)\n5. Ship Hero support ticket for lot/expiration associations\n\n### **Documentation Needed**\n\n* B2B Ship Hero integration roadmap (share separately with team)\n* Process documentation for Dish team on case breakdown\n\n### **Future Considerations**\n\n* B2B sales order creation in Ship Hero (Q4 target, not committed)\n* Transition to 88\\* SKU format (aligned with Dish transition timing)\n* Lead time validation for Arcadia vs Dish deliveries (confirmed: no change needed)\n\nNext Steps\n----------\n\n1. Monday finance meeting for final alignment\n2. Group sign-off via Slack/email (no additional meeting needed)\n3. Set go-live date after Monday approval\n4. Begin operationalization of transition plan",
