    "content": {
      "value": "1. TL;DR (executive summary)\n----------------------------\n\n* **Arcadia is a third-party frozen cold-storage 3PL** — legally *RMX Global Logistics*, running Blue Yonder WMS (portal \"ArcadiaOne\"). It is not a Wonder facility. In ShipHero it is modeled as its own warehouse.\n* **Function:** a frozen buffer / overflow node feeding DISH. Vendors and co-mans deliver 3P frozen product into Arcadia; Wonder then runs Arcadia → DISH replenishment transfers to keep DISH stocked while relieving DISH freezer capacity.\n* **The plan (2025):** fully automate *Vendor→Arcadia POs* and *Arcadia→DISH transfers* in **ShipHero + VDC**, with ShipHero as the system of record and perpetual inventory. Migrated off the old OrderGrid system in late 2025.\n* **What broke:** ShipHero inventory at Arcadia proved materially inaccurate (manual receiving, unrecorded B2B outbound, lot/expiry gaps). In Jan 2026 Wonder stopped treating ShipHero as the source of truth for Arcadia inv and switched to Arcadia's daily RMX snapshot (csvs).\n* **Current state (Jul 2026):** Arcadia is an active frozen buffer, but ordering and transfers are largely manual, coordinated daily in #vendor-to-dc slack channel. ShipHero still auto-generates the receiving PO, but inventory truth is RMX snapshot reconciled by hand for all planning systems.\n* **Direction:**\n* (a) SCC 88\\*→42\\* SKU cutover for Arcadia on Jul 14;\n* (b) VDC→POMS migration to a single PO/plan ledger;\n* (c) Arcadia is being replaced - decision between Lineage (3PL, EDI) and Linden (Wonder-operated, ShipHero) due Jul 13, target launch mid-August 2026.\n\n2. What Arcadia is\n------------------\n\n| Attribute | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Legal entity | RMX Global Logistics – Wonder @ Arcadia Cold Hazleton, LLC |\n| WMS | Blue Yonder (their portal = \"ArcadiaOne\"); not ShipHero - Arcadia declined ShipHero for Ops. Wonder mirrors transaction in SH for logs. |\n| ShipHero model | Separate warehouse than DISH |\n| Role | Frozen 3PL buffer / overflow node that replenishes DISH |\n| Inventory held | Frozen 3P / co-man goods, B2B, HDR crusts (1P), raw-material vendor SKUs |\n| Data feed to Wonder | Daily automated inventory snapshot email + received-PO snapshot (transaction detail only on request); vendor contact: Fernando Padilla |\n| Ordering cadence | Arcadia receives Mon–Fri only; transfer cadence Tue→Thu, Fri→Mon (no Saturday pickup) |\n\n3. How we got here (timeline: planned → pivots → current)\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n| Date | Event |\n| --- | --- |\n| Aug–Sep 2025 | VDC (\"Vendor-to-DC\") logic built to auto-generate PO quantities into DCs. VDC goes live but Arcadia ordering switched off pending inventory visibility. |\n| Sep–Oct 2025 | Formal Arcadia plan drafted (#arcadia-strategy). Interim: manually raise transfer orders to Arcadia, receive into DISH. Target go-live ~Oct. |\n| Oct 8 2025 | Brief Finance-driven halt — Arcadia PO creation/receiving paused pending Finance approval. |\n| Oct 21–28 2025 | Arcadia inventory bulk-uploaded to ShipHero (Sandbox→Prod); ShipHero support asked to retro-map lot/expiry from RMX sheet; UOM SKUs created (CS ships from Arcadia, 88\\*-EA received at DISH). Migrated off OrderGrid (OG data unreliable for months; OG wiped). |\n| ~Nov 3–4 2025 | First Arcadia→DISH transfers run (first automated report ~Nov 4; Emmett did a manual backup transfer Nov 3). \"Arcadia Go Live\" design doc published. |\n| Jan 9–13 2026 | PO-number collision discovered & fixed (see §6). Full-pallet replen loads into DISH mandated. |\n| Jan 14–22 2026 | THE PIVOTRed ShipHero dropped as source of truth for Arcadia inventory (\"materially inaccurate\"); switch to RMX daily snapshot; long-term intent = direct Blue Yonder integration. |\n| Feb 2026 | Decision to exit Arcadia (~3 months); RFPs for new frozen 3PL; plan to split B2B vs HDR into separate facilities; \"data-first\" RFP mandate. Interim ShipHero re-initialization compromise accepted. *(This exit timeline later slipped.)* |\n| May–Jun 2026 | VDC 2.0 live (incorporates DC delivery schedule). Freezer-relief program: route all 3P frozen to Arcadia, replenish DISH on a 7-day schedule; transfer coverage bumped +1 → +2 days. Recurring \"treat Arcadia as a vendor\" debate. |\n| Jun–Jul 2026 | SCC 88\\*→42\\* cutover; Arcadia = Phase 4B, Jul 14. VDC→POMS migration begins (unified PO/plan ledger). |\n| Jul 8–13 2026 | Lineage vs. Linden replacement discovery; decision due Jul 13, launch mid-Aug 2026. Order taxonomy already flags Arcadia→DISH transfers \"going away soon.\" |\n\n4. Current-state architecture (systems & data)\n----------------------------------------------\n\nwide1011 Vendors / Co-mans ARCADIA (RMX / Blue Yonder) DISH (ShipHero WMS)\n---------------- --------------------------- -------------------\nVendor POs ----------------> Physical receipt at Arcadia |--> Receipts mirrored in SH\n(created in ShipHero, (RMX books appt vs PO; but |\nCSV via VDC or manual) \"receives\" via inventory |\nadjustment, not true PO receipt)\n|\nDaily RMX snapshot email <-------------+ (= source of truth for inventory)\n-> shared inbox -> Drive -> BigQuery -> VDC\n|\nArcadia->DISH TRANSFER ORDER\n(created in ShipHero,CSV via VDC or manual);\n\"picked\" in SH to decrement actual shipped qty)\n|\nv SH auto-generates\n+----------------------------+\n| Receiving PO at DISH |--> DISH receives, relabels\n| (PO # matched Transfer # | VSKU -> 88\\*/42\\* EA,\n| | logs inv into DISH whs\n+----------------------------+\n\n**Systems in play:**\n\n* **ShipHero** — WMS / system of record for DISH; models Arcadia as warehouse 127552; auto-generates the receiving PO on every transfer. Not trusted for Arcadia on-hand.\n* **RMX daily snapshot** — de-facto source of truth for Arcadia inventory since Jan 2026.\n* **VDC (MRP)** — generates recommended vendor→Arcadia PO quantities and Arcadia→DISH transfer quantities; demand signal from LADLE's DISH forecast.\n* **BigQuery** — `int_ledger_purchase_orders`, raw ShipHero PO tables, `dish_inventory_snapshot`; ShipHero delta export now hourly (was 6h).\n* **POMS** — target unified PO/plan ledger (VDC→POMS migration in progress).\n* **SCC / Sporklift** — catalog + warehouse-routing; picks target warehouse from `command_center.sku_delivery_schedule`.\n\n5. Current workflows (step by step)\n-----------------------------------\n\n### A. Vendor → Arcadia (inbound PO)\n\n1. VDC generates recommended order quantities for vendor SKUs flagged for Arcadia. Flagging is now via the \"Delivery Locations\" section in Vendor Catalog (Arcadia must be added as a delivery location) — historically the `DC_ENDPOINT = 'ARCADIA'` flag.\n2. Sim posts a daily PO sheet in #vendor-to-dc (with a ShipHero-load tab). Procurement (Jenn Snyder / María Jumbo Flores) save the tab as CSV and load it as a PO in ShipHero, which emails the vendor.\n3. Vendor delivers to Arcadia (Mon–Fri); Arcadia books an appointment against the PO.\n4. In Arcadia's own WMS there is no true receipt against the PO - they do an inventory adjustment to bump quantity. So Wonder relies on ShipHe**ro** logs, not Arcadia's, for PO/receipt records.\n\n### B. Arcadia → DISH replenishment transfer\n\n1. VDC computes transfer quantity: demand over the order period − projected on-hand at receipt date, with +2 coverage days. Demand from LADLE's DISH (HDR) forecast.\n2. Sim posts the Arcadia→DISH transfer quantities in #vendor-to-dc; Emmett submits the order to Arcadia (daily cutoff).\n3. In ShipHero a transfer order is created. Emmett's team enters it on the day it arrives at DISH and systematically \"picks\" it via a desktop portal so Arcadia inventory decrements by what actually shipped (not what was ordered).\n4. The transfer auto-generates a receiving PO at DISH to receive against.\n5. DISH receives, then \"freezer pulls\" and relabels the VSKU to the Wonder 88\\*/42\\* each and logs into ShipHero.\n\n### C. DISH → Arcadia (reverse transfer, overflow — newer)\n\n1. Create an \"Arcadia outbound location\" in ShipHero, move items there, build a picking order (complicated by scan-to-pick not supporting location selection); OR\n2. **Cycle-count out** with reason code *\"transferred to Arcadia,\"* then create a separate PO to receive at Arcadia (needs confirmation these are excluded from waste numbers).\n\n### D. CK → Arcadia (production receiving — in progress)\n\nWork to add **Arcadia as a \"Customer\" in Supply Chain Portal** (for CK1 → Arcadia frozen pouches, e.g. marinara/bolo) is being pushed to prod but not fully live. SD1 UAT already \"dispatched CK1→SD1, Arcadia 3PL orders to SPORK.\"\n\n6. PO data flow & field mechanics\n---------------------------------\n\n**Four ways a PO appears in ShipHero for these flows:**\n\n1. **VDC (MRP)** → CSV upload into ShipHero (vendor POs).\n2. **Manual POs** created by Procurement/DISH ops (to \"find\" inventory).\n3. **POMS-created POs** (CK/ProdCo → DISH).\n4. **Transfer-generated POs** - an Arcadia→DISH transfer order **auto-creates a receiving PO at DISH**.\n\n**PO statuses:** `Pending` (open/editable, default), `Canceled` (void, kept for audit), `Closed` (manually closed on complete/partial receipt — closing is critical for forecasting accuracy). VDC additionally auto-closes overdue POs in its own logic (past lead time + `PO_AUTO_CLOSE_DAYS`) even while ShipHero still shows them Pending.\n\n**Vendor attribution problem (open):** Transfer POs carry broken vendor data - the `Warehouse Transfer` vendor resolves to **id = 0 / null** downstream.\n\n**BigQuery access:**\n\n* Transfers: `wonder-dw-prod-brd.inventory.int_ledger_purchase_orders` where `po like '%TO_DISH%' AND UPPER(ORDER_TYPE)='TRANSFER'`.\n* Raw ShipHero: `wonder-raw-prod.mysql_batch_sporklift.shiphero_purchase_orders` / `_purchase_order_items` (warehouse\\_id maps Arcadia/DISH/Millington).\n* Inventory: `wonder-sporklift-prod.sporklift.dish_inventory_snapshot`\n* Inventory current SOT: `wonder-dw-prod-brd`.`inventory.latest_arcadia_snapshot`\n\n**Vendor↔Wonder SKU mapping** lives in the Drive sheet \"3P Items to DISH and Arcadia\" (`dc_endpoint` = DISH/ARCADIA; `vendor_id`, `vendor_sku`, `pack_sku`).\n\n7. Planned vs. current — what changed and why\n---------------------------------------------\n\n| Dimension | Planned (2025) | Current (Jul 2026) | Why it changed |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Inventory source of truth | **ShipHero**, perpetual | **RMX daily snapshot**, reconciled manually | ShipHero Arcadia inventory materially inaccurate (phantom inv, unrecorded B2B outbound, lot/expiry gaps) |\n| Vendor→Arcadia POs | Fully automated via VDC | Semi-manual (VDC recommends → Procurement CSV-loads) | Data gaps; Arcadia doesn't truly receive vs PO |\n| Arcadia→DISH transfers | Automated transfer orders | ShipHero transfer order, but manually entered & \"picked\" | Need to decrement by actual shipped qty; avoid overstating |\n| B2B | Sales orders in ShipHero (Q4) | No SH order creation; manual depletion by reason code | Never prioritized; kept manual |\n| Vendor classification | Clean vendor per PO | Broken (`id=0`/null, multi-vendor) | \"Warehouse Transfer\" vendor unsupported downstream |\n| SKUs | 88\\* legacy | Migrating to 42\\* SCC (Arcadia Phase 4B, Jul 14) | Supply Chain Catalog rollout |\n| Long-term node | Keep Arcadia (ShipHero) | Replace Arcadia (Lineage vs Linden) | RMX service issues since ~Oct 2025, freezer constraints, SOX/SOC-1 needs |\n\n8. Known issues & risks (current)\n---------------------------------\n\n1. **Arcadia inventory in ShipHero is unreliable** — phantom inventory, unrecorded B2B outbound, lot/expiry mismatches. Mitigated by RMX snapshot reconciliation.\n2. **No Blue Yonder integration** — the intended long-term fix was never built.\n3. **Manual, error-prone flows** — transfers entered at arrival; B2B shipped manually; production receiving needed manual POs.\n4. **Broken vendor attribution** on transfer POs (id 0/null, multi-vendor).\n5. **On-order data gap** (lead time > order frequency) forces the VDC assumption workaround.\n6. **VDC over-ordering** during the relabel window when on-hand isn't respected.\n7. **Late transfer arrivals (~2–3 PM)** = unpickable same day → instock loss.\n8. **ShipHero allocation/locking** — support ticket **#339457** (stuck `TO-DISH_DTC…` / `PO-######` orders, \"hospital\" logic locking locations); requires stale-order cleanup.\n9. **SCC 42\\* cutover risk (Jul 14)** — Arcadia SKUs must exist in the Arcadia warehouse and POs switch to 42\\*; a **missing Arcadia delivery route** in `sku_delivery_schedule` already caused SPORK POs to default to Arcadia with a blank Ship-To (fixed by adding an Arcadia→DISH route).\n10. **Historical duplicate POs** still need renaming (Finance).\n11. **Double-counting risk** in the ProdCo roll-forward for Arcadia↔DISH transfers (Finance to trace a sample PO end-to-end).\n\n9. What's changing next\n-----------------------\n\n* **SCC 88\\*→42\\* cutover:** Arcadia begins receiving all new POs under new item numbers on Jul 14 (Phase 4B; DISH-side started Phase 4A Jul 7–8). All open POs re-keyed to 42\\*; FIFO + pallet isolation enforced.\n* **VDC → POMS:** unify plans + POs into a single POMS ledger; \"SKU duality\" (vendor SKU + Wonder UOM SKU together); PO creation/vendor-emailing stays in ShipHero/Sporklift for Phase 0. Note raw-material 5\\* SKUs never get 42\\*s.\n* **Arcadia replacement (decision due Jul 13, launch mid-Aug):**\n\n  + **Option A** — Lineage (3PL): cold-storage 3PL on Accellos One; integrate via EDI over AS2 (X12), CSV/portal fallback; SOX/BRC-compliant. Wonder's first EDI build. Recommended delivery = MVP (CSV) + fast-follow EDI.\n  + **Option B** — Linden (Wonder-operated): former BlueApron/FreshRealm facility on existing ShipHero WMS — \"architecturally the same as Arcadia\" (ShipHero POs + Sporklift transfer orders). Lower tech risk, higher labor lift.\n  + Both preserve the physical flow: frozen received at node → replenish DISH (where slacking happens) → cross-dock to IKC.",
